E-Commerce Sales Analysis Using SQL
Project Overview
This project focuses on analyzing an E-Commerce sales dataset using SQL to understand customer behavior, order patterns, product performance, revenue trends, and overall sales performance.
The analysis uses multiple related tables including customers, orders, order_items, products, and sales_cleaned. SQL queries are used to perform data quality checks, data validation, data manipulation, exploratory analysis, aggregations, joins, subqueries, and advanced analytical calculations.
The project demonstrates how SQL can be used to transform raw transactional data into meaningful business insights.
Dataset Description
The database contains information about customers, orders, products, order items, and cleaned sales transactions.
Main Tables
1. Customers
The customers table contains customer-level information.
Key columns include:
•	customer_id – Unique identifier for each customer
•	country – Customer's country
•	signup_date – Date when the customer registered
The analysis includes customer distribution by country, customer signup trends, customers without orders, and customer revenue contribution.
2. Orders
The orders table contains information about customer orders.
Key columns include:
•	order_id – Unique order identifier
•	customer_id – Customer associated with the order
•	order_date – Date of the order
•	status – Order status such as Completed, Cancelled, or Returned
The analysis examines order status distribution, customer order frequency, order dates, and relationships between customers and orders.
3. Order Items
The order_items table contains product-level details for each order.
Key columns include:
•	order_id – Associated order
•	product_id – Associated product
•	quantity – Quantity purchased
•	price – Price of the product
This table is used to calculate revenue, units sold, product performance, and order value.
4. Products
The products table contains information about products.
Key columns include:
•	product_id – Unique product identifier
•	product_name – Product name
•	category – Product category
The analysis uses this table to identify top-performing products and compare revenue and units sold across product categories.
5. Sales Cleaned
The sales_cleaned table contains cleaned and analysis-ready sales transaction data.
Important fields include:
•	order_id
•	product_id
•	quantity
•	price
•	Revenue
•	customer_id
•	order_date
•	status
•	year
•	month
The cleaned sales table is primarily used for revenue analysis, customer analysis, monthly trends, ranking, and advanced SQL analytics.
Data Quality and Validation
The project includes SQL-based data quality checks before performing analysis.
The following checks are performed:
•	Identification of missing values
•	Detection of duplicate records
•	Validation of customer IDs and product IDs
•	Validation of order information
•	Validation of quantity and price values
•	Standardization using TRIM
•	Validation of order dates against customer signup dates
•	Identification of potentially orphaned orders
•	Validation of completed, cancelled, and returned orders
The dataset documentation indicates that the original order data contains 1,000 orders, including 805 completed, 103 cancelled, and 92 returned orders. The cleaned sales data focuses on completed transactions.
