Business Analysis Performed
The SQL analysis focuses on several important business questions.
Customer Analysis
•	How many customers are present in each country?
•	How has customer signup changed over time?
•	Which customers have never placed an order?
•	How many orders has each customer placed?
•	What is the total revenue generated by each customer?
•	Which customers have the highest total spending?
Product Analysis
•	Which product categories generate the most revenue?
•	Which products sell the most units?
•	Which products generate the highest revenue?
•	What are the top 5 products by revenue?
•	How are products distributed across revenue quartiles?
Sales Analysis
•	What is the total revenue?
•	What is the total number of orders?
•	What is the average transaction revenue?
•	What is the monthly revenue trend?
•	How does revenue vary by country?
•	What is the minimum, average, and maximum order value?
Order Analysis
•	How many orders are completed, cancelled, or returned?
•	Which customers have placed the most orders?
•	What is the distribution of order values?
•	Which orders have high transaction values?
•	Are there orders associated with missing customer records?
Time-Based Analysis
The project performs time-based analysis using year and month fields.
This includes:
•	Monthly revenue trends
•	Customer signup trends
•	Month-over-month revenue changes
•	Running revenue totals
•	Revenue comparisons between consecutive months
